@startuml
title WINDOWED Redis (legacy filename: short-term)

actor Caller
participant Executor
participant "DistributedLock\n(optional)" as Lock
participant "Redis Repository" as Redis
participant StateMachine
participant Business
participant ResultPolicy

Caller -> Executor : execute(key, policy=WINDOWED)
opt short lock
  Executor -> Lock : acquire
end
Executor -> Redis : tryAcquire.lua\natomic state transition
Redis --> Executor : ACQUIRED / SUCCESS / PROCESSING / ...
opt short lock
  Executor -> Lock : release
end
Executor -> StateMachine : interpret

alt ACQUIRED
  StateMachine --> Executor : EXECUTE
  Executor -> Business : callback()
  Business --> Executor : value
  Executor -> ResultPolicy : capture
  Executor -> Redis : markSuccess.lua(owner,version,payload)
  Redis --> Executor : UPDATED
  Executor --> Caller : EXECUTED
else SUCCESS
  StateMachine --> Executor : REPLAY
  Executor -> ResultPolicy : replay
  Executor --> Caller : REPLAYED
else other
  StateMachine --> Executor : RETURN
  Executor --> Caller : state result
end

note over Redis
idempotencyWindow = semantic duplicate window
recordRetentionTtl = physical extra retention
When semantic window expires, a new generation may start
even if the Hash still physically exists.
end note
@enduml
